    "Data": {
      "Ticketid": "HF-1004",
      "Customername": "Jonah Kim",
      "Subject": "Two questions: monitor entitlement and guest wifi",
      "Body": "1) I moved to a hybrid schedule. Am I allowed a second monitor and a dock for home, and how do I order them? 2) We have an external auditor onsite next Tuesday through Thursday who needs wifi. What's the process and how long can her access last?",
      "Category": "Other",
      "Priority": "Low",
      "Rationale": "The ticket contains two low-impact informational requests spanning hardware entitlement and guest Wi-Fi, so I classified it as Other rather than forcing a single technical incident category. The draft is grounded in KB articles for laptop hardware and guest Wi-Fi, including entitlement, ordering path, manager approval, sponsorship URL, access scope, and duration. Confidence is high because both customer questions are directly covered.",
      "Confidence": 0.92,
      "Draftreply": "Hi Jonah,\n\nThanks for reaching out. For your hybrid schedule equipment and the auditor\u2019s guest Wi-Fi access:\n\n1. Docks and monitors: each employee is entitled to one dock and up to two 27-inch monitors. You can order them through the IT catalog, and the request will require manager approval.\n\n2. Guest Wi-Fi: sponsor the auditor from wifi.homefixsupply.com/guest. She will receive a code for the \"HomeFix-Guest\" network. Guest access is internet-only and does not provide access to internal HomeFix resources.\n\n3. Duration: guest codes are normally valid for 24 hours, but access can be extended to 5 days for auditors and contractors by any people-manager. That should cover Tuesday through Thursday if the extension is applied.\n\nBest regards,\nHomeFix Supply Support Team"
    }
